{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/7u90rih8","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":57.6,"top":235.2,"width":888,"height":384},"name":"Google Shape;113;p15","text":"THE CHOSEN PROBLEM\nPatients and caregivers leave hospital with dense instructions and must turn them into safe next steps at home.","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#171717","lineColor":"#333333","lineWidth":1.33,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#7ED957","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/wz214nyp","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":974.4,"top":235.2,"width":888,"height":384},"name":"Google Shape;114;p15","text":"PEOPLE AFFECTED\nPatients recovering at home and the family members helping manage their care.\n","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#171717","lineColor":"#333333","lineWidth":1.33,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#7ED957","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/h0bixsza","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":57.6,"top":648,"width":888,"height":384},"name":"Google Shape;115;p15","text":"WHY IT MATTERS\nMissing dose units, conflicting directions, or vague follow-up details can leave people unsure what to ask next.\n","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#171717","lineColor":"#333333","lineWidth":1.33,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#7ED957","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/uxkj2xgz","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":974.4,"top":648,"width":888,"height":384},"name":"Google Shape;116;p15","text":"PROBLEM STATEMENT\nHow might we help patients and caregivers understand discharge instructions and organize next steps without guessing when details are unclear?\n","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#171717","lineColor":"#333333","lineWidth":1.33,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#7ED957","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ofy9wn61","slideIndex":2,"text":""}
